r asks whether the owner lets the session use their computers and reach their other sessions — folders they share through Remote Control, sessions on their computers, and Claude Tag; its content_digest comes from a refusal that says this session may not reach its owner's other sessions or may not connect a computer yet, and allowing it limits the session to the owner's trusted devices for good. The service decides which card to show from the content_digest you pass. If the user says no, or the result says nothing was recorded, do not call it again unless the user asks you to; carry on without their computer and say what remains blocked.", "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__confirm_repository_trust", "schema": {"description": "Ask the session's owner a question only they can answer — in person, in the Claude app on a trusted device. You do not word the question and cannot answer it; the service shows the owner the details itself. No permission mode, stored rule or automation answers it. Do NOT ask in chat first; calling this tool IS the question. Call it ONLY with a content_digest a refusal gave you, exactly. There are two such questions. One asks whether the owner trusts what is attached to THIS session (its repositories, uploaded files, container image and project files); its content_digest comes from a refusal marked [repository_trust_required]. The other asks whether the owner lets the session use their computers and reach their other sessions — folders they share through Remote Control, sessions on their computers, and Claude Tag; its content_digest comes from a refusal that says this session may not reach its owner's other sessions or may not connect a computer yet, and allowing it limits the session to the owner's trusted devices for good. The service decides which card to show from the content_digest you pass. If the user says no, or the result says nothing was recorded, do not call it again unless the user asks you to; carry on without their computer and say 